{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_16-15-15-etcd_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v4.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 4,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"RawNode.Propose or serialized Node proposal handling reaches the current role. Followers forward to a known leader unless forwarding is disabled; candidates drop. The leader assigns current-term consecutive indexes, appends unstable entries, queues its own append response for persistence and broadcasts append messages anchored by previous index/term. A follower checks that anchor, appends only noncommitted conflicting suffix, bounds propagated commit to the matched extent and queues its reply through persistence. Term-filtered successful replies update peer Match. Active voter majority order statistics, or the minimum of both joint majorities, select a candidate index; leader commit advances only when that entry has its current nonzero term. Rejections, heartbeat-driven retries and snapshot fallback resynchronize lagging peers. Ready exposes committed entries only beyond the issued application frontier and blocks while a snapshot is outstanding; async delivery additionally requires locally stabilized entries. Advance or local apply response advances internal applied and frees budget. Node explicitly permits early Advance while external application runs, with inter-Ready application order left to the caller; this differs from the asynchronous response-after-apply contract. Client proposal return is only admission/Step outcome and can precede or never lead to commitment.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B_PROPOSE\",\n        \"B_ACK_QUEUE\",\n        \"B_ACK_CONSUME\",\n        \"B_COMMIT\",\n        \"B_READY\",\n        \"B_REPLICATION_SEND\",\n        \"B_STORAGE_FRONTIER\",\n        \"B_NODE_OWNER\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F_LOCAL_APPEND\",\n        \"F_DEFERRED_RESPONSE\",\n        \"F_MATCH\",\n        \"F_LEADER_COMMIT\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"src_raw_entry\",\n        \"src_leader_proposal\",\n        \"src_append_success\",\n        \"src_tracker\",\n        \"src_quorum_joint\",\n        \"src_majority\",\n        \"src_log_commit\",\n        \"src_log_append\",\n        \"src_append_handler\",\n        \"src_ready_accept\",\n        \"src_replication\",\n        \"src_replication_retry\",\n        \"src_log_delivery\",\n        \"src_log_frontiers\",\n        \"src_raw_advance\",\n        \"src_applied\",\n        \"src_node_loop\",\n        \"src_node_propose_wait\",\n        \"src_reset\",\n        \"src_election\",\n        \"src_send\",\n        \"src_raw_append\",\n        \"src_async_contract\",\n        \"src_step\",\n        \"src_progress_update\",\n        \"src_progress_reject\",\n        \"src_cfg_activation\",\n        \"src_ready_contract\",\n        \"src_raw_storage_tail\",\n        \"src_unstable_accept\",\n        \"src_unstable_stable\",\n        \"src_unstable_replace\",\n        \"src_async_config\",\n        \"src_node_restart\",\n        \"src_usage\",\n        \"src_startup\",\n        \"src_log_recover\",\n        \"src_changer\",\n        \"src_unstable_view_contract\",\n        \"src_storage_completion_contract\",\n        \"src_log_term_view\",\n        \"src_log_slice_view\",\n        \"src_readme_ready\",\n        \"src_example_ready\",\n        \"src_interaction_ready\",\n        \"src_test_node_ready\",\n        \"src_node_application_contract\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Ticks or Campaign enter hup, which checks promotability and unapplied configuration changes. Pre-election does not raise term; a real campaign increments term and records self Vote, with self response delayed for persistence. Vote grants check vote availability and log freshness. Candidate response type and active voter quorum determine win/loss. A winner resets progress and appends an empty current-term entry. Higher-term ordinary messages, election loss and configured quorum inactivity demote; lease/pre-vote exceptions are explicit. Transfer blocks new proposals, catches up the selected nonlearner and prompts a fresh election; timeout aborts transfer. Startup reconstructs log bounds and configuration from caller Storage, loads saved term/vote/commit and becomes follower. Snapshot restoration rejects obsolete or ineligible snapshots, fast-forwards a matching committed boundary, or installs snapshot history and configuration; a pending snapshot prevents promotion. Configuration activation uses validated simple changes or joint enter/leave, preserves progress for retained peers, initializes new progress at zero and handles configured leader removal. Application progress can initiate automatic joint exit.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B_ELECT\",\n        \"B_RESET\",\n        \"B_RECONSTRUCT\",\n        \"B_CONFIG\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F_LEADER_ROLE\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"src_election\",\n        \"src_step\",\n        \"src_transfer_roles\",\n        \"src_leader_proposal\",\n        \"src_log_commit\",\n        \"src_tracker\",\n        \"src_cfg_activation\",\n        \"src_startup\",\n        \"src_snapshot_restore\",\n        \"src_changer\",\n        \"src_restore_config\",\n        \"src_log_recover\",\n        \"src_applied\",\n        \"src_majority\",\n        \"src_quorum_joint\",\n        \"src_reset\",\n        \"src_pending_reads\",\n        \"src_read_tracker\",\n        \"src_log_restore\",\n        \"src_unstable_replace\",\n        \"src_bootstrap\",\n        \"src_raw_entry\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Term/role reset discards votes, peer progress and safe-read acknowledgment tracker while preserving local log and committed frontier. Self progress is initialized from local lastIndex, including potentially unstable inherited entries, so Match must not be equated with a fresh durable acknowledgment. Leader formation appends a current-term empty entry; commit requires the selected entry term to equal the leader term, preventing the old self frontier alone from authorizing new-term commitment. Active membership changes reinterpret retained progress and can re-evaluate commit; new peers begin Match=0. Stale-term replies do not advance leader support or stabilize entries. Local append completion additionally matches entry term/index; a later current-term append message can reconfirm outstanding writes. Committed state and application acknowledgments survive term changes: apply responses are term zero, snapshot completion can be processed despite stale term, and applied uses a monotonic maximum. Pending pre-commit read requests survive reset but enter the new read-only mechanism only after current-term commitment; existing safe-read acknowledgment state is reset. Recovery starts as follower with caller-supplied persisted prefix and configuration, not restored leadership. The accepted follower append history is represented by the unstable overlay until replacement writes are reflected safely in Storage. Storage-completion validation controls when queries fall through to Storage: message raft term and entry term/index are distinct context checks. This persistence boundary feeds both term-based support validation and election log freshness.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B_RESET\",\n        \"B_CONFIG\",\n        \"B_ACK_CONSUME\",\n        \"B_COMMIT\",\n        \"B_READY\",\n        \"B_STORAGE_FRONTIER\",\n        \"B_RECONSTRUCT\",\n        \"B_READ_CONTEXT\",\n        \"B_ACCEPT_HISTORY\",\n        \"B_LOG_VIEW\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F_MATCH\",\n        \"F_LEADER_COMMIT\",\n        \"F_ACCEPTED_HISTORY\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"src_reset\",\n        \"src_step\",\n        \"src_cfg_activation\",\n        \"src_ready_accept\",\n        \"src_unstable_stable\",\n        \"src_startup\",\n        \"src_changer\",\n        \"src_log_recover\",\n        \"src_log_delivery\",\n        \"src_raw_storage_tail\",\n        \"src_applied\",\n        \"src_pending_reads\",\n        \"src_read_tracker\",\n        \"src_election\",\n        \"src_leader_proposal\",\n        \"src_transfer_roles\",\n        \"src_raw_entry\",\n        \"src_restore_config\",\n        \"src_append_success\",\n        \"src_progress_update\",\n        \"src_progress_reject\",\n        \"src_replication\",\n        \"src_tracker\",\n        \"src_quorum_joint\",\n        \"src_majority\",\n        \"src_log_commit\",\n        \"src_ready_contract\",\n        \"src_log_frontiers\",\n        \"src_raw_advance\",\n        \"src_raw_append\",\n        \"src_unstable_accept\",\n        \"src_unstable_replace\",\n        \"src_async_config\",\n        \"src_snapshot_restore\",\n        \"src_log_restore\",\n        \"src_bootstrap\",\n        \"src_replication_retry\",\n        \"src_unstable_view_contract\",\n        \"src_storage_completion_contract\",\n        \"src_log_term_view\",\n        \"src_log_slice_view\",\n        \"src_append_handler\",\n        \"src_log_append\",\n        \"src_unstable_term_view\",\n        \"src_node_application_contract\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Synchronous documentation overlap wording remains unresolved; persist-before-send is the explicit Ready field contract and common safe caller policy.\",\n      \"Lease-read timing assumptions and full read response construction remain open; safe-read context production/consumption is traced only to explain old pending work.\",\n      \"Caller crash atomicity, durable storage implementations beyond MemoryStorage, and application snapshot coordination are external boundaries requiring a concrete harness policy for a future question.\",\n      \"Node early Advance and pending configuration activation are a newly identified interface boundary: internal applied bookkeeping can precede external application, so campaign/proposal applicability must use the selected entry contract.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative proposal-to-application and authority/recovery paths now connect through actual producers, consumers, eligibility and persistence handoffs. Usability is a sourced navigation judgment, not a safety proof or full variant coverage.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"c79ba43cc6bc49cf8f2775b10983fdeb\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"c79ba43cc6bc49cf8f2775b10983fdeb\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"dfac2ae9789d47