{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '135,187p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '261,280p' ../agent-source/doc.go; sed -n '1280,1338p' ../agent-source/raft.go; cat submission.json; cat ../submission.schema.json\"","aggregated_output":"\tTick()\n\t// Campaign causes the Node to transition to candidate state and start campaigning to become leader.\n\tCampaign(ctx context.Context) error\n\t// Propose proposes that data be appended to the log. Note that proposals can be lost without\n\t// notice, therefore it is user's job to ensure proposal retries.\n\tPropose(ctx context.Context, data []byte) error\n\t// ProposeConfChange proposes a configuration change. Like any proposal, the\n\t// configuration change may be dropped with or without an error being\n\t// returned. In particular, configuration changes are dropped unless the\n\t// leader has certainty that there is no prior unapplied configuration\n\t// change in its log.\n\t//\n\t// The method accepts either a pb.ConfChange (deprecated) or pb.ConfChangeV2\n\t// message. The latter allows arbitrary configuration changes via joint\n\t// consensus, notably including replacing a voter. Passing a ConfChangeV2\n\t// message is only allowed if all Nodes participating in the cluster run a\n\t// version of this library aware of the V2 API. See pb.ConfChangeV2 for\n\t// usage details and semantics.\n\tProposeConfChange(ctx context.Context, cc pb.ConfChangeI) error\n\n\t// Step advances the state machine using the given message. ctx.Err() will be returned, if any.\n\tStep(ctx context.Context, msg pb.Message) error\n\n\t// Ready returns a channel that returns the current point-in-time state.\n\t// Users of the Node must call Advance after retrieving the state returned by Ready (unless\n\t// async storage writes is enabled, in which case it should never be called).\n\t//\n\t// NOTE: No committed entries from the next Ready may be applied until all committed entries\n\t// and snapshots from the previous one have finished.\n\tReady() <-chan Ready\n\n\t// Advance notifies the Node that the application has saved progress up to the last Ready.\n\t// It prepares the node to return the next available Ready.\n\t//\n\t// The application should generally call Advance after it applies the entries in last Ready.\n\t//\n\t// However, as an optimization, the application may call Advance while it is applying the\n\t// commands. For example. when the last Ready contains a snapshot, the application might take\n\t// a long time to apply the snapshot data. To continue receiving Ready without blocking raft\n\t// progress, it can call Advance before finishing applying the last ready.\n\t//\n\t// NOTE: Advance must not be called when using AsyncStorageWrites. Response messages from the\n\t// local append and apply threads take its place.\n\tAdvance()\n\t// ApplyConfChange applies a config change (previously passed to\n\t// ProposeConfChange) to the node. This must be called whenever a config\n\t// change is observed in Ready.CommittedEntries, except when the app decides\n\t// to reject the configuration change (i.e. treats it as a noop instead), in\n\t// which case it must not be called.\n\t//\n\t// Returns an opaque non-nil ConfState protobuf which must be recorded in\n\t// snapshots.\n\tApplyConfChange(cc pb.ConfChangeI) *pb.ConfState\n\nThis implementation is up to date with the final Raft thesis\n(https://github.com/ongardie/dissertation/blob/master/stanford.pdf), although our\nimplementation of the membership change protocol differs somewhat from\nthat described in chapter 4. The key invariant that membership changes\nhappen one node at a time is preserved, but in our implementation the\nmembership change takes effect when its entry is applied, not when it\nis added to the log (so the entry is committed under the old\nmembership instead of the new). This is equivalent in terms of safety,\nsince the old and new configurations are guaranteed to overlap.\n\nTo ensure that we do not attempt to commit two membership changes at\nonce by matching log positions (which would be unsafe since they\nshould have different quorum requirements), we simply disallow any\nproposed membership change while any uncommitted change appears in\nthe leader's log.\n\nThis approach introduces a problem when you try to remove a member\nfrom a two-member cluster: If one of the members dies before the\nother one receives the commit of the confchange entry, then the member\n\t\tr.trk.Visit(func(id uint64, pr *tracker.Progress) {\n\t\t\tif id != r.id {\n\t\t\t\tpr.RecentActive = false\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t\treturn nil\n\tcase pb.MsgProp:\n\t\tif len(m.Entries) == 0 {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Panicf(\"%x stepped empty MsgProp\", r.id)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif r.trk.Progress[r.id] == nil {\n\t\t\t// If we are not currently a member of the range (i.e. this node\n\t\t\t// was removed from the configuration while serving as leader),\n\t\t\t// drop any new proposals.\n\t\t\treturn ErrProposalDropped\n\t\t}\n\t\tif r.leadTransferee != None {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Debugf(\"%x [term %d] transfer leadership to %x is in progress; dropping proposal\", r.id, r.Term, r.leadTransferee)\n\t\t\treturn ErrProposalDropped\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tfor i := range m.Entries {\n\t\t\te := &m.Entries[i]\n\t\t\tvar cc pb.ConfChangeI\n\t\t\tif e.Type == pb.EntryConfChange {\n\t\t\t\tvar ccc pb.ConfChange\n\t\t\t\tif err := ccc.Unmarshal(e.Data); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tpanic(err)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tcc = ccc\n\t\t\t} else if e.Type == pb.EntryConfChangeV2 {\n\t\t\t\tvar ccc pb.ConfChangeV2\n\t\t\t\tif err := ccc.Unmarshal(e.Data); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tpanic(err)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tcc = ccc\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif cc != nil {\n\t\t\t\talreadyPending := r.pendingConfIndex > r.raftLog.applied\n\t\t\t\talreadyJoint := len(r.trk.Config.Voters[1]) > 0\n\t\t\t\twantsLeaveJoint := len(cc.AsV2().Changes) == 0\n\n\t\t\t\tvar failedCheck string\n\t\t\t\tif alreadyPending {\n\t\t\t\t\tfailedCheck = fmt.Sprintf(\"possible unapplied conf change at index %d (applied to %d)\", r.pendingConfIndex, r.raftLog.applied)\n\t\t\t\t} else if alreadyJoint && !wantsLeaveJoint {\n\t\t\t\t\tfailedCheck = \"must transition out of joint config first\"\n\t\t\t\t} else if !alreadyJoint && wantsLeaveJoint {\n\t\t\t\t\tfailedCheck = \"not in joint state; refusing empty conf change\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\tif failedCheck != \"\" && !r.disableConfChangeValidation {\n\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x ignoring conf change %v at config %s: %s\", r.id, cc, r.trk.Config, failedCheck)\n\t\t\t\t\tm.Entries[i] = pb.Entry{Type: pb.EntryNormal}\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tr.pendingConfIndex = r.raftLog.lastIndex() + uint64(i) + 1\n\t\t\t\t\ttraceChangeConfEvent(cc, r)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n{\n  \"action\": \"explore\",\n  \"question\": \"With actual public Node configuration proposals, does the pending-change guard follow ApplyConfChange activation or the internal applied frontier advanced by Node.Advance, when configuration activation is deliberately deferred?\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Compare three explicit caller policies from independently constructed one-voter prefixes: defer ApplyConfChange and withhold Advance; defer ApplyConfChange but call Advance early; and activate first before Advance. A real election and first ProposeConfChange produce the committed entry. All Ready persistence finishes before Advance and no network message is delivered early. Public Node.Status acts as an event-loop barrier after proposal/Advance processing. A second actual configuration proposal reveals whether it is encoded as a configuration entry or replaced by an empty normal entry; record commitment separately. In the early policy, later committed entries are not applied until the first configuration activation completes, and all delivered configuration entries are eventually activated in order. Whether the general Node.Advance overlap permission includes delayed configuration activation remains an explicit semantic question, so observations are conditional and not a finding. New peers are not running and their network traffic is dropped; an uncommitted second proposal in a control is not a liveness failure. Finite Ready deadlines diagnose only driver incompletion.\",\n  \"harness_path\": \"early_advance_explore_test.go\",\n  \"feedback\": {\n    \"ref_ids\": [\n      \"src_node_application_contract\",\n      \"src_node_status_apply\",\n      \"src_ready_accept\",\n      \"src_raw_advance\",\n      \"src_leader_proposal\",\n      \"src_membership_contract\"\n    ],\n    \"answered\": \"The source distinguishes Node early-Advance permission from the stricter wording of RawNode.Advance. The prepared experiment uses Node directly, so no lower-level permission is silently substituted. It also separates internal Applied, actual returned ApplyConfChange calls, encoded second-entry type and commitment; none is inferred from ProposeConfChange returning nil.\",\n    \"remaining\": [\n      \"Observe the three policy outcomes in the clean-copy execution, then retain the precise contract applicability gap or formulate a sourced scoped responsibility if justified.\"\n    ],\n    \"understanding\": \"unchanged\",\n    \"rationale\": \"This single comparison isolates the completion signal consumed by pendingConfIndex guards while preserving actual producer history and inter-Ready application order. No second arbitrary schedule is needed before reading its outcome.\"\n  }\n}{\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"ArtifactReviewItem\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"target_id\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Target Id\"\n        },\n        \"aspect\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"applicability\",\n            \"decomposition\",\n            \"checker_correspondence\"\n          ],\n          \"title\": \"Aspect\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"status\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"no_issue_found\",\n            \"needs_reading\",\n            \"disputed\",\n            \"revision_needed\"\n          ],\n          \"title\": \"Status\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"source_ids\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"rationale\": {\n          \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"report_title\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"description\": \"Optional short Chinese reading title for this target; presentation only, never a verdict\",\n          \"title\": \"Report Title\"\n        },\n        \"report_answer\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"description\": \"Optional Chinese observed-answer summary preserving applicability; numbers and status come from retained assessment\",\n          \"title\": \"Report Answer\"\n        },\n        \"counterevidence\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Counterevidence\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"limitations\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Limitations\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"challenged_components\": {\n          \"description\": \"Components requiring repair, distinct from the review aspect; revision_needed must name them\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"configuration\",\n              \"initialization\",\n              \"driver\",\n              \"observation\",\n              \"oracle\",\n              \"expectation\",\n              \"scope\"\n            ],\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Challenged Components\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"aspect\",\n        \"status\",\n        \"source_ids\",\n        \"rationale\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"ArtifactReviewItem\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"AuditQuestion\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"description\": \"Sourced investigation, protections and unknowns; neither a requirement nor a finding.\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"minimum\": 1,\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Audit Spec Version\"\n        },\n        \"disposition\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"enum\": [\n                \"explained_by_existing_mechanism\",\n                \"concrete_suspicion\",\n                \"needs_specific_evidence\",\n                \"ready_for_check\"\n              ],\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Disposition\"\n        },\n        \"preferred_check\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"enum\": [\n                \"source_review\",\n                \"direct_test\",\n                \"controlled_schedule\",\n                \"local_model\"\n              ],\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Preferred Check\"\n        },\n        \"question\": {\n          \"title\": \"Question\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"importance\": {\n          \"title\": \"Importance\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"source_ids\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"participants\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Participants\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"objects\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Objects\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"contexts\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Contexts\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"event_paths\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Event Paths\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"activity_classes\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"A1\",\n              \"A2\",\n              \"A3\",\n              \"A4\",\n              \"A5\",\n              \"A6\",\n              \"A7\"\n            ],\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Activity Classes\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"behavior_ids\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Behavior Ids\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"fact_ids\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Fact Ids\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"additionalProperties\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"description\": \"Behavior ID to sourced prehistory, context or consequence support; not a direct principal Fact edge\",\n          \"title\": \"Supporting Behavior Ids\",\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"enum\": [\n                \"establishment\",\n                \"preservation\",\n                \"consumption\",\n                \"recovery\"\n              ],\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Obligation Relation Kind\"\n        },\n        \"counterevidence\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Counterevidence\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"unknowns\": {\n          \"description\": \"Specific unresolved premises or discriminators of this question; not generic caution or a checklist of untested cases\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Unknowns\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"priority\": {\n          \"default\": 0,\n          \"description\": \"System consequence and audit significance, justified in importance; not proof\",\n          \"maximum\": 3,\n          \"minimum\": 0,\n          \"title\": \"Priority\",\n          \"type\": \"integer\"\n        },\n        \"trigger_rationale\": {\n          \"title\": \"Trigger Rationale\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"question\",\n        \"importance\",\n        \"trigger_rationale\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"AuditQuestion\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"BindingAssociation\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"claim_id\": {\n          \"title\": \"Claim Id\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"source_ids\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"rationale\": {\n          \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"claim_id\",\n        \"source_ids\",\n        \"rationale\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"BindingAssociation\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"BindingDraft\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"associations\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/BindingAssociation\"\n          },\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"title\": \"Associations\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"anchor\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CodeAnchor\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null\n        },\n        \"id\": {\n          \"title\": \"Id\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"material_id\": {\n          \"title\": \"Material Id\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"symbol\": {\n          \"description\": \"Source symbol tied to a verified declaration, interface member or explicitly declared call-site anchor. The behavior range may be a narrow internal snippet. Do not substitute arbitrary words from the excerpt.\",\n          \"title\": \"Symbol\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"start_line\": {\n          \"title\": \"Start Line\",\n          \"type\": \"integer\"\n        },\n        \"end_line\": {\n          \"title\": \"End Line\",\n          \"type\": \"integer\"\n        },\n        \"description\": {\n          \"title\": \"Description\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"pending\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Pending\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"associations\",\n        \"id\",\n        \"material_id\",\n        \"symbol\",\n        \"start_line\",\n        \"end_line\",\n        \"description\",\n        \"pending\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"BindingDraft\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"CandidateSubmission\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"rationale\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"sources\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRange\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Sources\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"feedback\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ResearchFeedback\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null\n        },\n        \"repair_of\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"description\": \"Rejected operation ID whose complete draft this submission repairs\",\n          \"title\": \"Repair Of\"\n        },\n        \"map_path\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Map Path\"\n        },\n        \"map_changes\": {\n          \"additionalProperties\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/UnderstandingChange\"\n          },\n          \"default\": {},\n          \"title\": \"Map Changes\",\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        },\n        \"reconnect_questions\": {\n          \"additionalProperties\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/AuditQuestion\"\n          },\n          \"description\": \"Optional explicit question reconnections; changing an accepted Unit proposition still requires F2/F3\",\n          \"title\": \"Reconnect Questions\",\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        },\n        \"action\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"continue\",\n            \"pause\",\n            \"explained\",\n            \"obligation\"\n          ],\n          \"title\": \"Action\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"candidate_id\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Candidate Id\"\n        },\n        \"parent_candidate_id\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Parent Candidate Id\"\n        },\n        \"question\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/AuditQuestion\"\n        },\n        \"resume_conditions\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Resume Conditions\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"result_implications\": {\n          \"additionalProperties\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"default\": {},\n          \"propertyNames\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"holds\",\n              \"violated\",\n              \"incomplete\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Result Implications\",\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        },\n        \"obligation\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ClaimDraft\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null\n        },\n        \"bindings\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/BindingDraft\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Bindings\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"rationale\",\n        \"action\",\n        \"question\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"CandidateSubmission\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"CheckSubmission\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"rationale\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"sources\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRange\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Sources\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"feedback\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ResearchFeedback\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null\n        },\n        \"repair_of\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"description\