{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The three policies produced different results: early `Advance` allowed the second configuration entry to commit before the first configuration was activated. Withholding `Advance` caused the second proposal to become an empty normal entry; activating the first configuration required support from the added voter. I’ll retain these observations as conditional results: whether the API permits deferring `ApplyConfChange` across `Advance` remains unresolved.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat early_advance_explore_test.go; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('../logs/6dab32606865456a91887dbe509c632f/stdout.log'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if 'CA_EVENT' in d.get('Output',''): print(d['Output'].strip())\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(s['\"'$defs'\"']['ResearchFeedback'],indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat early_advance_explore_test.go; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('../logs/6dab32606865456a91887dbe509c632f/stdout.log'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if 'CA_EVENT' in d.get('Output',''): print(d['Output'].strip())\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(s['\"'$defs'\"']['ResearchFeedback'],indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"package raft\n\nimport (\n    \"context\"\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"testing\"\n    \"time\"\n\n    pb \"go.etcd.io/raft/v3/raftpb\"\n)\n\nfunc TestAssuranceNodeEarlyAdvanceConfiguration(t *testing.T) {\n    for _, policy := range []string{\"deferred_no_advance\", \"deferred_early_advance\", \"applied_then_advance\"} {\n        t.Run(policy, func(t *testing.T) {\n            emit := func(v map[string]interface{}) {\n                v[\"policy\"] = policy\n                b, err := json.Marshal(v)\n                if err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n                fmt.Println(\"CA_EVENT \" + string(b))\n            }\n            ms := NewMemoryStorage()\n            if err := ms.ApplySnapshot(pb.Snapshot{Metadata: pb.SnapshotMetadata{Index:1, Term:1,\n                ConfState:pb.ConfState{Voters:[]uint64{1}}}}); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n            if err := ms.SetHardState(pb.HardState{Term:1, Commit:1}); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n            n := RestartNode(&Config{ID:1, ElectionTick:10, HeartbeatTick:1, Storage:ms,\n                Applied:1, MaxSizePerMsg:1024*1024, MaxInflightMsgs:16})\n            defer n.Stop()\n            ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 5*time.Second)\n            defer cancel()\n            receive := func() Ready {\n                select {\n                case rd := <-n.Ready(): return rd\n                case <-ctx.Done(): t.Fatal(\"driver Ready deadline exceeded\"); return Ready{}\n                }\n            }\n            save := func(rd Ready) {\n                if !IsEmptySnap(rd.Snapshot) {\n                    if err := ms.ApplySnapshot(rd.Snapshot); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n                }\n                if err := ms.Append(rd.Entries); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n                if !IsEmptyHardState(rd.HardState) {\n                    if err := ms.SetHardState(rd.HardState); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n                }\n                // Outbound messages to not-yet-running new peers are dropped.\n                // Persistence always precedes any possible message delivery.\n            }\n            advance := func() Status { n.Advance(); return n.Status() }\n            applyConfig := func(e pb.Entry) {\n                if e.Type != pb.EntryConfChange { t.Fatalf(\"unexpected config type %s\", e.Type) }\n                var cc pb.ConfChange\n                if err := cc.Unmarshal(e.Data); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n                n.ApplyConfChange(cc)\n            }\n            if err := n.Campaign(ctx); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n            for i := 0; i < 12; i++ {\n                st := n.Status()\n                if st.RaftState == StateLeader && st.Applied >= 2 { break }\n                rd := receive(); save(rd); advance()\n                if i == 11 { t.Fatal(\"initial producer prefix did not finish\") }\n            }\n            firstCC := pb.ConfChange{Type:pb.ConfChangeAddNode, NodeID:2}\n            if err := n.ProposeConfChange(ctx, firstCC); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n            var first pb.Entry\n            var firstReady Ready\n            for i := 0; i < 12; i++ {\n                rd := receive(); save(rd)\n                for _, e := range rd.CommittedEntries {\n                    if e.Type == pb.EntryConfChange { first, firstReady = e, rd }\n                }\n                if first.Index != 0 { break }\n                advance()\n                if i == 11 { t.Fatal(\"first committed configuration not delivered\") }\n            }\n            _ = firstReady\n            activatedFirst := false\n            if policy == \"applied_then_advance\" { applyConfig(first); activatedFirst = true }\n            if policy != \"deferred_no_advance\" { advance() }\n            before := n.Status()\n            emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"before_second\", \"first_index\":first.Index,\n                \"first_activated\":activatedFirst, \"internal_applied\":before.Applied,\n                \"commit\":before.Commit, \"voters\":before.Config.Voters.IDs()})\n            secondCC := pb.ConfChange{Type:pb.ConfChangeAddNode, NodeID:3}\n            if err := n.ProposeConfChange(ctx, secondCC); err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n            // Status is a public event-loop barrier after proposal processing.\n            afterProposal := n.Status()\n            emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"second_proposal_processed\", \"first_index\":first.Index,\n                \"first_activated\":activatedFirst, \"internal_applied\":afterProposal.Applied,\n                \"commit\":afterProposal.Commit, \"voters\":afterProposal.Config.Voters.IDs()})\n            if policy == \"deferred_no_advance\" {\n                applyConfig(first); activatedFirst = true; advance()\n            }\n            rd := receive(); save(rd)\n            var second pb.Entry\n            for _, e := range rd.Entries {\n                if e.Index > first.Index { second = e; break }\n            }\n            if second.Index == 0 { t.Fatal(\"no second proposal entry reached Ready\") }\n            emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"second_entry\", \"first_index\":first.Index,\n                \"first_activated\":activatedFirst, \"second_index\":second.Index,\n                \"entry_type\":second.Type.String(), \"entry_data_bytes\":len(second.Data)})\n            st := advance()\n            emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"second_stored\", \"first_index\":first.Index,\n                \"first_activated\":activatedFirst, \"second_index\":second.Index,\n                \"commit\":st.Commit, \"internal_applied\":st.Applied, \"voters\":st.Config.Voters.IDs()})\n            if policy == \"deferred_early_advance\" {\n                // Observe the second committed batch but do not apply it before\n                // the first. This preserves the documented inter-Ready order.\n                committedReady := receive(); save(committedReady)\n                emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"before_activation\", \"first_index\":first.Index,\n                    \"first_activated\":activatedFirst, \"commit\":n.Status().Commit,\n                    \"committed_count\":len(committedReady.CommittedEntries)})\n                applyConfig(first); activatedFirst = true\n                for _, e := range committedReady.CommittedEntries {\n                    if e.Type == pb.EntryConfChange { applyConfig(e) }\n                }\n                advance()\n            }\n            final := n.Status()\n            emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"finished\", \"first_activated\":activatedFirst,\n                \"commit\":final.Commit, \"internal_applied\":final.Applied,\n                \"voters\":final.Config.Voters.IDs()})\n            // Stopping with an uncommitted second proposal is a finite controlled\n            // endpoint, not a liveness failure or a claim that it must commit.\n        })\n    }\n}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"before_second\",\"first_activated\":false,\"first_index\":3,\"internal_applied\":2,\"policy\":\"deferred_no_advance\",\"voters\":{\"1\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"second_proposal_processed\",\"first_activated\":false,\"first_index\":3,\"internal_applied\":2,\"policy\":\"deferred_no_advance\",\"voters\":{\"1\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"entry_data_bytes\":0,\"entry_type\":\"EntryNormal\",\"event\":\"second_entry\",\"first_activated\":true,\"first_index\":3,\"policy\":\"deferred_no_advance\",\"second_index\":4}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"second_stored\",\"first_activated\":true,\"first_index\":3,\"internal_applied\":3,\"policy\":\"deferred_no_advance\",\"second_index\":4,\"voters\":{\"1\":{},\"2\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"finished\",\"first_activated\":true,\"internal_applied\":3,\"policy\":\"deferred_no_advance\",\"voters\":{\"1\":{},\"2\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"before_second\",\"first_activated\":false,\"first_index\":3,\"internal_applied\":3,\"policy\":\"deferred_early_advance\",\"voters\":{\"1\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"second_proposal_processed\",\"first_activated\":false,\"first_index\":3,\"internal_applied\":3,\"policy\":\"deferred_early_advance\",\"voters\":{\"1\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"entry_data_bytes\":6,\"entry_type\":\"EntryConfChange\",\"event\":\"second_entry\",\"first_activated\":false,\"first_index\":3,\"policy\":\"deferred_early_advance\",\"second_index\":4}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":4,\"event\":\"second_stored\",\"first_activated\":false,\"first_index\":3,\"internal_applied\":3,\"policy\":\"deferred_early_advance\",\"second_index\":4,\"voters\":{\"1\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":4,\"committed_count\":1,\"event\":\"before_activation\",\"first_activated\":false,\"first_index\":3,\"policy\":\"deferred_early_advance\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":4,\"event\":\"finished\",\"first_activated\":true,\"internal_applied\":4,\"policy\":\"deferred_early_advance\",\"voters\":{\"1\":{},\"2\":{},\"3\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"before_second\",\"first_activated\":true,\"first_index\":3,\"internal_applied\":3,\"policy\":\"applied_then_advance\",\"voters\":{\"1\":{},\"2\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"second_proposal_processed\",\"first_activated\":true,\"first_index\":3,\"internal_applied\":3,\"policy\":\"applied_then_advance\",\"voters\":{\"1\":{},\"2\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"entry_data_bytes\":6,\"entry_type\":\"EntryConfChange\",\"event\":\"second_entry\",\"first_activated\":true,\"first_index\":3,\"policy\":\"applied_then_advance\",\"second_index\":4}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"second_stored\",\"first_activated\":true,\"first_index\":3,\"internal_applied\":3,\"policy\":\"applied_then_advance\",\"second_index\":4,\"voters\":{\"1\":{},\"2\":{}}}\nCA_EVENT {\"commit\":3,\"event\":\"finished\",\"first_activated\":true,\"internal_applied\":3,\"policy\":\"applied_then_advance\",\"voters\":{\"1\":{},\"2\":{}}}\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"New sourced answers and next discriminators; historical remaining is not current pending work.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"ref_ids\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Ref Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"answered\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Answered\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"remaining\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Remaining\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"understanding\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"updated\",\n            \"unchanged\",\n            \"deferred\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Research understanding across turns, not a declaration that this submission changes the map\",\n      \"title\": \"Understanding\"\n    },\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"question_updates\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QuestionUpdate\"\n      },\n      \"default\": {},\n      \"title\": \"Question Updates\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"ref_ids\",\n    \"answered\",\n    \"remaining\",\n    \"rationale\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"ResearchFeedback\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns={'action':'research','rationale':'Retain the completed three-policy Node exploration without promoting a conditional caller schedule into a property violation. The source and execution isolate internal application acknowledgment from configuration activation; the next limiting premise is API permission, not another execution of the same schedule.','feedback':{'ref_ids':['6dab32606865456a91887dbe509c632f','src_node_application_contract','src_node_status_apply','src_ready_accept','src_raw_advance','src_leader_proposal','src_membership_contract'],'answered':'Exploration 6dab32606865456a91887dbe509c632f completed all three independent policies. Each starts from an explicit one-voter MemoryStorage snapshot and uses actual RestartNode, Campaign, ProposeConfChange, Ready, Advance, Status and ApplyConfChange calls. The first add-voter configuration is committed at index 3. With activation and Advance withheld, internal Applied stays 2 and the second proposal is emitted at index 4 as an empty EntryNormal; activation occurs only after that proposal is processed. With activation deferred but Advance called, Applied becomes 3 while voters remain {1}; the second proposal is an EntryConfChange at index 4 and commits before the first activation, still with voters {1}. The caller then activates both configurations in order and finishes with commit/Applied 4 and voters {1,2,3}. With first activation before Advance, the second configuration entry is accepted but commitment remains 3 with voters {1,2}, since voter 2 is absent. These are separate histories, not one combined execution. All Ready writes precede Advance; outbound traffic to absent peers is dropped; no internal raft state is assigned. MemoryStorage substitutes for crash-durable storage in a no-crash exploration. Public Status barriers and returned ApplyConfChange calls distinguish internal App